<title>USA: Vans stake cut by N.Y. group.</title>
<headline>Vans stake cut by N.Y. group.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>A group including Zweig-DiMenna Partners L.P., a New York investment partnership, said Thursday it cut its stake in Vans Inc to 649,000 common shares or 4.9 percent from six percent held previously.</p>
<p>In a filing with the Securities and Exchange Commission, the group said its latest transactions include the sale of 134,900 common shares on February 18 at a price of $13.6157 per share.</p>
<p>Vans is an Orange, Calif.,-based maker of casual shoes.</p>
